This manifest defines the implemented HOTT/Identity fragment. It does not
claim complete Higher Observational Type Theory. Surface Eq, refl, transport,
general dependent lifting, Universe action, univalence, and effectful identity
remain outside this fragment.

An internal relation-family goal is immutable and is identified by category,
exact left and right carrier IS_TYPE Claims, exact left and right HAS_TYPE
Claims, and Context bridge. The carrier Claims may differ for dependent
fibers. Unsupported heterogeneous carrier action is residual, not an invalid
goal. A goal stores no selected rule, search state, source position,
conversion cache, or witness.

Action requests are immutable and graph-consed by their complete typed keys.
Action results are separate records keyed by request ID. Context,
Substitution, Operation, Claim, Derivation, action, certificate, and work IDs
never occur in object Term identity.

CONTEXT, SUBSTITUTION, RELATION_TYPE, and TERM are compiler-local
parametricity actions. They establish relation preservation for accepted
terms. They are not themselves object Identity and are excluded from artifact
identity roots.

IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION and OBJECT_TERM are object-language actions.
IDENTITY_TYPE_COMPUTATION is keyed by an exact source IS_TYPE Claim and an
OBJECT_IDENTITY Context bridge. OBJECT_TERM is keyed by an exact source
HAS_TYPE Claim, the same bridge, and the exact type-action request for its
classifier. Their certificates retain endpoint Claims, the acted classifier,
the ordinary witness Term and Claim, and the Derivation DAG needed by replay.
No action ID occurs in the object witness Term.

A Context bridge is one shared span representation for endpoint
substitutions. EMPTY_IDENTITY is the unique empty-telescope identity.
PARAMETRIC_RELATION classifies compiler-local relation extensions.
OBJECT_IDENTITY classifies extensions by exact object action families and
ordinary witness Claims. Graph shape alone never upgrades a
PARAMETRIC_RELATION bridge to OBJECT_IDENTITY.

The object action uses the semantic DIMENSION_ACTION Core former and the
operator contract in dimension_action_v1.schema. A dimension operator is the
only authority for source dimension, target dimension, face restrictions, and
composition. Repeated higher action composes or extends operators. There are
no dimension-specific Term tags, fixed boundary tables, generated identity
TypeDeclarations, or generated constructor ordinals.

The initial object identity family of A is DIMENSION_ACTION(A,e_0), where e_0
is the canonical extension from dimension zero to dimension one. Its boundary
applications are ordinary APP nodes in canonical face order. Acting again
uses e_1, e_2, and so on. A fully applied acted family denotes its center;
partial boundary application remains an ordinary dependent function.

DIMENSION_ACTION_TYPE_FORMATION proves the acted family head has its exact
dependent boundary classifier. Ordinary APP_ELIM and
IS_TYPE_FROM_HAS_TYPE prove the fully boundary-applied family is a type.
DIMENSION_ACTION_TERM proves that acting on an ordinary typed Term produces a
Term in the exact acted classifier. DIMENSION_ACTION_CONSTRUCTOR validates an
acted constructor against the source TypeDeclaration, source constructor
ordinal, source field telescope, operator, and acted Context prefix.
DIMENSION_ACTION_THUNK_RETURN_WITNESS validates the admitted pure
THUNK(RETURN(v)) witness without allocating a declaration.

TypeDeclarationDB is authority only for source-defined and imported ADT/IADT
schemas. Object action reads those schemas through a read-only acted view. It
must not allocate a TypeDeclaration, synthesize a generated origin, assign a
new constructor ordinal, or reconstruct a second semantic schema from
readback metadata.

Type action for Gamma |- A type constructs the endpoint Context and relation
family under the exact left and right substitutions. The compiler-local
family uses the ordinary THUNK(LAMBDA(...RETURN...)) representation of a
dependent family. Certificate replay checks its body under an explicit
binding correspondence. It is not authority for object Identity.

Relation instantiation is one typed operation shared by diagonal Term action
and candidate materialization. It reindexes exact endpoint and carrier Claims,
constructs endpoint Context extensions, specializes the relation body, and
publishes its exact IS_TYPE Claim. Candidate materialization returns an exact
witness Claim, EMPTY_FAMILY, or RESIDUAL. A READY plan alone is never a
witness.

RELATION_TYPE(A0,A1,a0,a1) and RELATION_WITNESS(a0,a1) encode the current
compiler-local relation action. A witness Term stores no action ID and is not
evidence without its accepted HAS_TYPE Claim and Derivation. These forms do
not extend global DefEq and are not serialized as object Identity roots.

Type-former dispatch is selected by one declarative descriptor. Ordinary ADT,
pure Pi, empty-effect computation, pure Thunk, and relation-higher actions are
admitted for the listed compiler-local fragment. Object action uses the
generic dimension mechanism for supported ADT/IADT, nondependent pure Pi,
pure Return/Thunk, Lambda, APP, nullary Match, and guarded induction
hypothesis cases. The dispatcher must publish RESIDUAL or UNSUPPORTED for all
other cases and must not fall back to parametricity evidence.

For a nondependent pure Pi, object Identity is pointwise. Related endpoint
functions must send two related inputs to related results. The result is a
direct dependent Pi classifier over x0, x1, and their acted-family witness; it
is not wrapped in an auxiliary declaration. Certificate replay uses binding
identity and alpha correspondence, never physical binder allocation order.
Dependent codomains remain residual until family lifting is represented and
replayed.

Object action for a typed THUNK(LAMBDA(x,body)) is derivation-driven. It
extends the bridge by x0, x1, and the input witness, composes endpoint
substitutions, and recursively acts on the body. A pure APP(FORCE(f),x) body
acts on f and x and applies the pointwise witness. Intermediate sequencing may
use zero-clause COMPUTATION_FOLD nodes. Effectful APP remains residual.

Object action for THUNK(RETURN(v)) reads accepted THUNK_INTRO and RETURN_INTRO
premises, acts on v, and constructs the generic acted witness for v0, v1, and
vR. The exact classifier is obtained by applying the acted source classifier
to the endpoint thunk values. No generated declaration or generated-schema
validator participates.

Constructor action is incremental and telescope-directed. Each source field
contributes its endpoint values and acted field witness in dependency order.
Later classifiers are reindexed through the already acted prefix. The source
constructor identity remains the source declaration and ordinal; the action
Term records the source constructor and operator instead of inventing another
constructor namespace.

Object action for an admitted Match is derivation-driven. It acts on the exact
scrutinee Claim and each branch body under the branch Context bridge. Its
motive is the exact acted family instantiated at endpoint Matches.
Convertible source motives require an explicit CONVERSION Derivation. Pattern
fields, general dependent motives, and effectful branches remain residual
unless their exact action and replay rules are present.

INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS action requires an accepted source
INDUCTION_HYPOTHESIS_ELIM Claim and the acted recursive argument. It does not
recursively invoke the enclosing Match action and therefore cannot introduce
a Derivation cycle. IH frame identity is distinct from binding identity and is
never silently renamed.

For the compiler-local relation action, same-constructor ADT witnesses retain
one accepted field-witness Claim per argument. Distinct constructors produce
EMPTY_FAMILY, not a Boolean result and not compiler contradiction. APP,
LAMBDA, Match, Return, Thunk, and IH relation witnesses retain their exact
accepted child Claims. This is relation preservation, not object Identity
authority.

A substitution action owns a naturality certificate for both endpoint
squares under an exact pure conversion profile and deterministic step budget.
Exhaustion is residual and never equality. Reindexing along an identity
substitution returns the original Claim and must not create a self-premised
Derivation.

Implemented object-action boundary:

- ordinary ADT/IADT schema and constructor action: executable through the
  read-only source declaration and generic dimension operator;
- nondependent pure Pi: executable pointwise;
- dependent Pi: residual;
- pure Return and pure Thunk: executable for the admitted derivations;
- Lambda and APP: executable for the admitted pure derivation fragment;
- Match and induction hypothesis: executable for the admitted guarded
  derivation fragment;
- empty-effect computation: executable only through the listed pure forms;
- effectful or unresolved computation, operation request, and computation
  fold handler semantics: residual;
- resource-sensitive terms: residual until usage action is represented;
- Universe and host primitive: unsupported in fragment version 6.

Artifact persistence stores only accepted ordinary object evidence: source
Claims, semantic dimension operators, acted-family Claims, witness Claims,
and their reachable Derivation DAG. Compiler-local relation actions,
certificates, work queues, residual search state, normalization fuel, and
allocation history are absent. Replay reconstructs semantic operators from
their inline vectors and validates every acted classifier and witness without
search or semantic-arena mutation.

Family formation and family inhabitation are distinct. An acted family can be
well formed without an inhabitant. Failure to execute an unsupported action
does not prove the family empty. Successful object evidence never changes
DefEq, conversion policy, or TypeDeclaration authority.

This fragment demonstrates closed homogeneous one-dimensional object Identity
and selected repeated higher actions through the same generic operator. It
does not establish general coherence, transport, symmetry, composition,
Universe identity, univalence, contextual-equivalence completeness, or full
Higher Observational Type Theory.
